		<name>SuperAwesomeMagicalMusic</name>
		<summary>Jellyfin first, with YouTube Music, Qobuz, SiriusXM, radio and Android Auto</summary>
		<desc>&lt;p&gt;A music player for self-hosters. It plays from your &lt;b&gt;Jellyfin&lt;/b&gt; library first and fills the gaps from &lt;b&gt;YouTube Music&lt;/b&gt; or &lt;b&gt;Qobuz&lt;/b&gt;; artists you're missing are added to &lt;b&gt;Lidarr&lt;/b&gt;. It also plays &lt;b&gt;SiriusXM&lt;/b&gt; (live channels, Xtra channels and Pandora artist stations) and local &lt;b&gt;radio&lt;/b&gt;, and works in &lt;b&gt;Android Auto&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Made for the road&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Separate bitrates for Wi-Fi, cellular and satellite (T-Satellite and other direct-to-cell services), and a cap for Android's Data Saver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dead-zone cache that fetches the next songs while the signal is good, and downloads for offline listening that upgrade themselves to better copies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In Android Auto: bookmark a song with one tap and pick its playlist later on the phone, thumbs up and down on Pandora stations, restart or rewind SiriusXM songs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Listening&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Even volume across services, lyrics (Jellyfin or LRCLIB), a sleep timer, an equalizer and a home-screen widget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Playlists synced to your Nextcloud (sign in through the browser, so SSO works), and playlist import from YouTube and Spotify links.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Listening history, including songs heard on SiriusXM, and scrobbling to ListenBrainz and Last.fm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every account is your own: the app talks directly to your servers and services. SiriusXM, YouTube Music and Qobuz are reached through their unofficial or private APIs, which can change without notice.&lt;/p&gt;
</desc>
